rows.40:464c:
Back then, the captain of the girls' swim club was a girl named Yuko Seto.
She was a famous swimmer who held a whole bunch of records. She won on her own, of course, and she led this school to team championships again and again.
The school got so crazy about the girls' swim club that there was even a plan to build a new pool behind the new school building.{p}

rows.40:476c:
The swim club did have a boys' side too, but their results were kind of so-so. They didn't have many members either, and they always had to practice while giving way to the girls.
The incident happened during the summer vacation of Seto's third year.
Seto already had a university recommendation lined up, so even after the other third-years retired from the club, she never missed practice.{p}

rows.40:48c0:
That day was clear and hot, they say.
On days like that, being in the water feels so good, doesn't it?
Unlike the girls, who were training like crazy for the meet after summer vacation, the boys seemed like they were mostly just having fun splashing around.{p}

rows.40:4bb4:
They opened the pool gate and let the stray dog in.
They wanted to give Seto a scare.
She was always tearing into them and they never talked back, so it was meant as a little payback.{p}

rows.40:4e14:
They all screamed and scattered, they say.
As far as the boys were concerned, the plan was a success.
Watching those stuck-up girls run around squealing seemed funny, and kind of cute.{p}

rows.40:5734:
Listen, {c}{f:|}.
No matter how good you are at the dog paddle, you can't do it in this pool.
If you trampled all over my sister's feelings after everything she did...{p}

rows.40:57d0:
Hee hee hee, I wonder what I'd do~.
...Well, that's the end of my story.
On to the next person.{p}

rows.40:5834:
That's right, people started hearing someone swimming in the pool when nobody was there.
Splash, splash, like that.
And you know, when that happens...{p}

rows.40:5f28:
Splash, splash.
Soft at first, then louder.
Until it sounded like someone drowning...{p}

rows.40:62b4:
It wasn't Seto who'd been holding a hand up out of the pool water.
Hayashi screamed because she saw a girl who looked exactly like her, reaching out from under the water.
The figure was wearing a sailor uniform, and it was translucent, wavering back and forth.{p}
